invariant: INV-14
file: srv_auth.c
catches: srv_auth_test
reason: the RSA cap test asks for CH_RSA_MODULUS_MAX instead of the
  modulus length in pub_len, so a server whose key is smaller than the
  build's ceiling refuses a buffer its own signature fits in. An RSA-PSS
  signature is exactly as long as the modulus, which is what makes the
  exact test possible at all. test/srv_auth_test.c signs with an
  RSA-2048 key into a buffer of exactly 256 bytes and requires CH_OK.
  The cast keeps the mutant compiling: with the ceiling in place the
  identity is the one thing this function stops reading.

--- old
    return id->pub_len;
--- new
    (void)id;
    return SRV_SIG_MAX;
